{{also|persécuté|persécute}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|sekʷ|id=follow}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|persécuter}}, from {{der|en|EL.|persecutor}}, from {{der|en|la|persequor|persequor, persecutus|follow up, pursue}}, from {{prefix|la|per|sequor|t1=through|t2=follow|nocat=1}} (English {{m|en|sequel}}). Compare {{m|en|prosecute}}. Cf. also {{m|en|pursue}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈpɝsəkjut/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Mélange a trois-persecute.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|persecut}}

# To pursue in a manner to injure, grieve, or afflict; to [[beset]] with cruelty or [[malignity]]; to harass; especially, to afflict, harass, punish, or put to death for one's race, sexual identity, adherence to a particular religious creed, or mode of worship.
#: {{ux|en|He who persecutes one will persecute all.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|book=Matthew|chapter=5|verse=44|passage="Do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and '''persecute''' you."}}
# To harass with [[importunity]]; to pursue with persistent [[solicitations]]; to annoy.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|oppress}}, {{l|en|harass}}, {{l|en|distress}}, {{l|en|worry}}, {{l|en|annoy}}

